1. Install required packages

sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
sudo apt install --no-install-recommends xserver-xorg x11-xserver-utils xinit openbox chromium unclutter -y

2. Disable screen blanking + power saving
sudo nano /etc/xdg/openbox/autostart

a)paste

xset s off
xset -dpms
xset s noblank

unclutter -idle 0

3. Create kiosk startup script



nano ~/kiosk.sh


b)Paste this EXACTLY:



#!/bin/bash

# Disable screen blanking
xset s off
xset -dpms
xset s noblank

# Hide mouse cursor
unclutter -idle 0 &

# Give the desktop time to load
sleep 2

# Launch CTA display
chromium \
    --kiosk \
    --start-fullscreen \
    --window-size=800,480 \
    --window-position=0,0 \
    --force-device-scale-factor=1 \
    --noerrdialogs \
    --disable-infobars \
    --disable-session-crashed-bubble \
    --disable-translate \
    --user-data-dir=/home/spypi/cta-kiosk \
    --incognito \
    "http://www.transitchicago.com/diydisplay/?s1=41220&size=big&w=0"





b) save the file

c)Make it executable:

chmod +x ~/kiosk.sh

4. Auto-start X session in kiosk mode

nano ~/.bash_profile

Add to the bottom 

startx ~/kiosk.sh



5. Make sure Raspberry Pi boots to console (important)

sudo raspi-config

System Options → Boot / Auto Login → Console Autologin


6. Reboot

sudo reboot
